{# Layer toggle strip — sticky band that lets the visitor flip between the
   four reading states (Neutral / Light / Dark / Both).

   Renders as an inline strip, not a floating widget. Place wherever the
   choice would feel earned on the page — typically below the lead/hero.

   Drives:
   - .layer-stage classes via site.js
   - The .lens-aside [data-layer] reveals

   See LAYERS.md.
#}
<aside class="layer-toggle-strip"
       role="region"
       aria-label="Reading lens">
  <div class="layer-toggle-strip__controls" role="group" aria-label="Side toggles">
    <button class="layer-toggle-strip__btn"
            type="button"
            data-layer="light"
            aria-pressed="false">
      <span class="layer-toggle-strip__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>Light side</span>
    </button>
    <button class="layer-toggle-strip__btn"
            type="button"
            data-layer="dark"
            aria-pressed="false">
      <span class="layer-toggle-strip__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      <span>Dark side</span>
    </button>
  </div>
  <p class="layer-toggle-strip__summary" data-layer-summary aria-live="polite">
    standard view
  </p>
</aside>
